From: CodeAndSolder <codeandsolder@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: page_pool: compare DMA index bit count explicitly

PP_DMA_INDEX_BITS is an integer-valued constant expression built from a
conditional operator. Passing the value directly to likely()/unlikely()
causes GCC 14.4 to diagnose -Wint-in-bool-context with CONFIG_WERROR=y
when building page_pool.c on the IPQ5332 arm64 target.

Test the bit count against zero explicitly. This preserves the compile-
time behavior for every supported bit count and keeps WERROR enabled.

---
--- a/net/core/page_pool.c
+++ b/net/core/page_pool.c
@@ -479,7 +479,7 @@
 	int err = 0;
 	u32 id;
 
-	if (unlikely(!PP_DMA_INDEX_BITS))
+	if (unlikely(PP_DMA_INDEX_BITS == 0))
 		goto out;
 
 	/*
@@ -521,7 +521,7 @@
 	 */
 	dma = page_pool_get_dma_addr_netmem(netmem);
 
-	if (likely(PP_DMA_INDEX_BITS)) {
+	if (likely(PP_DMA_INDEX_BITS != 0)) {
 		id = netmem_get_dma_index(netmem);
 		if (!id)
 			return;
@@ -752,7 +752,7 @@
 
 	__page_pool_unmap_netmem_dma(pool, netmem);
 	page_pool_set_dma_addr_netmem(netmem, 0);
-	if (likely(PP_DMA_INDEX_BITS))
+	if (likely(PP_DMA_INDEX_BITS != 0))
 		netmem_set_dma_index(netmem, 0);
 }
 
